-names></name><name><surname>Emerson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Limpaphayom</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Safety, acceptability, and feasibility of a single-visit approach to cervical-cancer prevention in rural Thailand: a demonstration project</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>2003</year><volume>361</volume><fpage>814</fpage><lpage>820</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0140-6736(03)12707-9</pub-id>doi<!--PubMed citation query: 'Lancet||361|814||bib8|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12642047</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sankaranarayanan</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Wesley</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title/><source>A Practical Manual On Visual Screening for Cervical Neoplasia</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>Lyon: IARC Press</publisher-name>IARC Technical Publication No. 41</citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sankaranarayanan</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Budukh</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Rajkumar</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effective screening programmes for cervical cancer in low- and middle-income developing countries</article-title><source>Bull World Health Organ</source><year>2001</year><volume>79</volume><fpage>954</fpage><lpage>962</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Bull World Health Organ||79|954||bib10|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11693978</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sankaranarayanan</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Nene</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name><name><surn